{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "People over the age of 65 must retake their driving test every 5 years",
        "additional_details": "I believe older people need to have the examiner in the car to assess how they drive and then make the decision as to whether they are still fit to drive. I have had experience of an accident caused by an older driver and I believe regular tests for older drivers may be an important step towards greater safety on the roads.",
        "background": "I think at the age of 65 you should have a retake of your driving test and continue doing so every 5 years. I don\u2019t feel a renewal of a driving license and providing medical records are quite enough.",
